---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { extractFaqItems } from '../utils/schema-helpers';
import { withSiteUtm } from '../lib/site-utm.mjs';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const themeGeneratorHref = withSiteUtm('https://themes.powerbi.tips', 'theme-cite');
const layoutsGalleryHref = withSiteUtm('https://tools.powerbi.tips/themes/gallery', 'theme-cite');

const title = 'Power BI Theme Generator: free JSON themes for reports';
const description = 'What is the Power BI Theme Generator?';

// Owned H2 + five FAQ H3s. extractFaqItems reads this string; do not add
// Entity as ## / ### (that heading would become a junk FAQPage item).
const citeFaqMarkdown = `## What is the Power BI Theme Generator?

**TL;DR.** PowerBI.tips Theme Generator is a free visual editor that writes valid Power BI theme JSON (colors, text, icons, and visual properties) plus gallery layouts. Built for report authors who do not want to hand-write the file. Download the JSON and import it in Desktop.

### What is a Power BI theme JSON file?

A Power BI theme is a JSON file that sets colors, fonts, icons, and visual properties so every page looks the same. Desktop can set a simple palette. A full theme file goes much deeper, and that file is hard to write by hand.

### How do I import a theme into Power BI Desktop?

Download the JSON from the generator. In Desktop go to View → Themes → Browse for themes and pick the file. Apply the theme before you customize visual properties on the page, or those overrides will block the theme.

### Is the PowerBI.tips Theme Generator free?

Yes. Building and downloading a theme is free. Saving a library of themes is TipsPlus. Layout and PBIR downloads from the gallery are free.

### What’s the difference between the generator and the layout gallery?

The generator builds the theme JSON (colors, text, icons, properties). The gallery gives you starting layouts and PBIR files you open in Desktop. Use both: theme for brand, layout for page structure.

### Why did my theme fail Microsoft validation?

In February 2023 Microsoft tightened theme validation so uploads must match the schema. Files that used to load can fail. The generator emits files that match the current validation rules.
`;

const faqItems = extractFaqItems(citeFaqMarkdown);
const faqJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: item.question,
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: item.answer,
    },
  })),
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={faqJsonLd}>
  <article>
    <section class="mb-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-neutral-900">{title}</h1>
    </section>

    <section class="prose max-w-none">
      <h2>What is the Power BI Theme Generator?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>TL;DR.</strong> PowerBI.tips Theme Generator is a free visual editor that writes valid
        Power BI theme JSON (colors, text, icons, and visual properties) plus gallery layouts. Built
        for report authors who do not want to hand-write the file. Download the JSON and import it in
        Desktop.
      </p>
    </section>

    <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4">
        <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">What</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-700">
          A free visual editor that writes a valid Power BI report theme JSON (colors, text, icons,
          properties), plus gallery layouts.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4">
        <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Who</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-700">
          Report authors who want branded, consistent reports without hand-writing JSON.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4">
        <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Cost</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-700">
          Generator is free. Theme library save is TipsPlus. Layout / PBIR downloads from the gallery
          are free.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white p-4">
        <dt class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">Not</dt>
        <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-700">
          Not Microsoft. Not Power BI Desktop. Not a paid-only studio.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <section class="prose max-w-none mt-10">
      <h3>What is a Power BI theme JSON file?</h3>
      <p>
        A Power BI theme is a JSON file that sets colors, fonts, icons, and visual properties so every
        page looks the same. Desktop can set a simple palette. A full theme file goes much deeper, and
        that file is hard to write by hand.
      </p>

      <h3>How do I import a theme into Power BI Desktop?</h3>
      <p>
        Download the JSON from the generator. In Desktop go to View → Themes → Browse for themes and
        pick the file. Apply the theme before you customize visual properties on the page, or those
        overrides will block the theme.
      </p>

      <h3>Is the PowerBI.tips Theme Generator free?</h3>
      <p>
        Yes. Building and downloading a theme is free. Saving a library of themes is TipsPlus. Layout
        and PBIR downloads from the gallery are free.
      </p>

      <h3>What’s the difference between the generator and the layout gallery?</h3>
      <p>
        The generator builds the theme JSON (colors, text, icons, properties). The gallery gives you
        starting layouts and PBIR files you open in Desktop. Use both: theme for brand, layout for page
        structure.
      </p>

      <h3>Why did my theme fail Microsoft validation?</h3>
      <p>
        In February 2023 Microsoft tightened theme validation so uploads must match the schema. Files
        that used to load can fail. The generator emits files that match the current validation rules.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a
        class="rounded-full bg-blue-600 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-blue-700"
        href={themeGeneratorHref}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Open the Theme Generator
      </a>
      <a
        class="rounded-full bg-neutral-100 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-neutral-900 hover:bg-neutral-200"
        href={layoutsGalleryHref}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Get free layouts
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-neutral-700">
      Related:
      <a class="font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800" href={`${base}/2021/12/22/power-bi-themes/`}>Power BI Themes</a>,
      <a class="font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800" href={`${base}/2023/02/28/powerbi-tips-theme-generator-the-ultimate-tool-for-creating-complex-themes/`}>PowerBI Tips Theme Generator: The Ultimate Tool for Creating Complex Themes</a>,
      <a class="font-medium text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800" href={`${base}/2026/09/02/power-bi-layouts-pbir-gallery/`}>Power BI Layouts Have Evolved: Download PBIR Files from the Gallery</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
